+FINDING src/cart/cart.js:4 | Leftover `console.log('DEBUG ...')` prints the full cart lines on every total; it's noisy in production and leaks customer cart contents into logs. Remove it.
+FINDING src/cart/cart.js:5 | Commented-out sort/reduce code (lines 5-6) is dead code with no explanation. Git history already keeps it, so delete it.
+FINDING src/cart/price.js:2 | The null/type/negative-qty guards (lines 2-4) repeat checks that `src/api/validate.js` already does at the API boundary (per CLAUDE.md, code behind the boundary gets well-formed lines). They also fail silently: a malformed line is priced at 0 (free) instead of raising an error, which hides upstream bugs. Remove them, or throw if a guard is really wanted.
+FINDING src/cart/price.js:1 | `discountPercent` is never validated, here or at the boundary (validate.js only checks lines). A value over 100 gives negative line totals, a negative value raises the price, and a non-number like undefined-from-JSON or a string gives NaN totals. Validate it to a finite number in [0, 100] at the API boundary.
+FINDING src/cart/price.js:6 | The discount is rounded per line, so the cart's total discount depends on how the items are split into lines (e.g. 3 lines of 4c at 10%: each line's 0.4c rounds to 0c, so the discount is 0c instead of 1c on the 12c subtotal). If the discount is meant for the whole order, apply and round it once on the cart subtotal.
+FINDING src/cart/totalV2.js:3 | `cartTotalV2` copies `cartTotal` just to add a discount parameter, so there are now two total functions that can drift apart, and the original `cartTotal` silently ignores discounts. Add an optional `discountPercent` to `cartTotal` instead of a parallel "V2" module.
+FINDING src/cart/price.js:1 | The commit adds no tests for the new discount logic (rounding, 0%/100%, the boundary cases), even though the project uses `node --test` and has no test files yet.
+VERDICT: changes
